### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and Visual Studio / Rider.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### 1. Log in as the seeded admin (Development password from appsettings.Development.json)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### The token from the login response, used by the requests below
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 2. Who am I (roles + permissions)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Register a new user (gets the default "User" role)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jane.doe",
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "password": "Password1",
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Doe"
}

### 4. Users, paged and searchable
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10&search=jo
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Roles
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Permission catalog for a role editor
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Create a role
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "User Manager",
  "description": "Can view and edit users",
  "permissions": [
    { "module": "Users", "action": "View" },
    { "module": "Users", "action": "Edit" }
  ]
}

### 8. Exercise catalog: shared exercises plus your own custom ones
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Muscles, equipment and exercise types the exercises refer to by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/muscles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/equipment
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/exercise-types
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Create a custom exercise (ids from the lists above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sled Push",
  "description": "Push a weighted sled across the floor",
  "instructions": "Lean into the handles\nDrive with the legs",
  "typeId": 1,
  "primaryMuscleIds": [19],
  "secondaryMuscleIds": [10]
}
